Derived work notice
-------------------
blockads-linux is a Linux port inspired by and partially derived from
blockads-android (https://github.com/pass-with-high-score/blockads-android),
Copyright (C) the blockads-android authors, licensed under the GNU General
Public License v3.0. The derived parts keep that licence and its copyright
notices; the modifications are Copyright (C) 2026 MateusBMP. Derived parts:

  * The filter-list rule parser (src/blockads_linux/filters/parser.py) is a
    port of tunnel/internal/trie/parser.go and compiler.go.
  * The custom-rule parser (src/blockads_linux/filters/custom_rules.py) is a
    port of app/.../utils/CustomRuleParser.kt.
  * The bundled filter catalog (src/blockads_linux/filters/data/catalog.json)
    and DNS-over-HTTPS blocklist (data/doh_blocklist.txt) are generated from
    app/src/fdroid/assets/preset/default_filters.json and
    app/src/main/assets/blocklist_doh.txt.
  * The query decision order and blocked answers
    (src/blockads_linux/daemon/pipeline.py, responses.py) follow
    tunnel/engine_dns_server.go, engine_standalone.go and engine_dns_query.go
    (serveDNS, standaloneBlock, isUpstreamBlocked, domainHasAAAA).
  * SafeSearch / YouTube Restricted matching (daemon/safesearch.py) is a port
    of tunnel/internal/safesearch/safesearch.go.
  * DNS stamp handling (daemon/upstream/stamps.py) follows
    tunnel/internal/dns/stamp.go; the DNS provider presets and their addresses
    (daemon/upstream/presets.py) come from
    app/.../data/entities/DnsProvider.kt.
  * Test vectors in tests/unit/test_pipeline.py and test_stamps.py are ported
    from tunnel/dns_server_test.go, dns_order_test.go,
    internal/safesearch/safesearch_test.go and internal/dns/stamp_test.go.

